<!-- Plugin Configuration File. Read more: https://plugins.jetbrains.com/docs/intellij/plugin-configuration-file.html -->
<idea-plugin>
    <id>com.github.devvikassoni.leaklens</id>
    <name>LeakLens: Android Memory Leak Detector &amp; AI Fix Assistant</name>
    <vendor email="vikasacsoni9211@gmail.com" url="https://github.com/dev-vikas-soni">Vikas Soni</vendor>

    <description><![CDATA[
        <h2><b>Stop Out-of-Memory (OOM) errors before they reach your users.</b></h2>
        <p><b>LeakLens</b> is the ultimate <b>Android Studio Plugin</b> for <b>Memory Leak Detection</b> and <b>Heap Analysis</b>. It brings the power of LeakCanary’s <b>Shark engine</b> directly into your IDE, enhanced with <b>AI-powered fix suggestions</b> (OpenAI/Gemini).</p>

        <h3><b>🚀 Why LeakLens?</b></h3>
        <p>Tired of switching between your app, Logcat, and Profiler? LeakLens automates the workflow to find, analyze, and fix <b>Android memory leaks</b> in real-time.</p>

        <h3><b>🛠️ Core SEO Features</b></h3>
        <ul>
            <li><b>🔍 Deep Heap Analysis:</b> Capture heap dumps from devices or import <b>.hprof</b> files for instant Shark-powered analysis.</li>
            <li><b>🤖 AI Fix Engine:</b> Use <b>GPT-4o</b> or <b>Gemini Pro</b> to explain complex leak traces and generate <b>Kotlin/Java code fixes</b>.</li>
            <li><b>🛡️ Preventive Inspections:</b> 6+ <b>Static Analysis (UAST)</b> inspections catch leaks <i>as you write code</i> (e.g., Static Activity Refs, Inner Class Leaks).</li>
            <li><b>📊 Real-time Memory Monitor:</b> A built-in graph to track <b>Android JVM Heap</b> usage and trigger auto-dumps when thresholds are hit.</li>
            <li><b>💡 Smart Fix Suggestions:</b> Actionable templates for 11+ common patterns like <b>Context leaks</b>, <b>View Binding</b>, and <b>Handler</b> leaks.</li>
            <li><b>🎯 One-Click Trace Navigation:</b> Click any part of the leak trace to jump directly to the problematic line in your source code.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3><b>✅ Compatible With</b></h3>
        <ul>
            <li><b>Languages:</b> 100% support for <b>Kotlin</b> and <b>Java</b>.</li>
            <li><b>Frameworks:</b> Optimized for <b>Jetpack Compose</b>, Fragments, ViewModels, and Coroutines.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3><b>📊 How we compare</b></h3>
        <table>
            <tr>
                <td><b>Feature</b></td>
                <td><b>LeakLens</b></td>
                <td><b>Profiler</b></td>
                <td><b>LeakCanary</b></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>IDE Integrated</td>
                <td>✅ Full</td>
                <td>✅ Partial</td>
                <td>❌ External App</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>AI Fix Assistant</td>
                <td>✅ Yes</td>
                <td>❌ No</td>
                <td>❌ No</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>No Dependency</td>
                <td>✅ Yes</td>
                <td>✅ Yes</td>
                <td>❌ Requires SDK</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Static Analysis</td>
                <td>✅ Real-time</td>
                <td>❌ No</td>
                <td>❌ No</td>
            </tr>
        </table>

        <p><i>If LeakLens helps you save hours of debugging, please consider leaving a <b>5-star review</b>! It helps us keep the tool free and updated.</i></p>
    ]]></description>

    <change-notes><![CDATA[
